; ABA (Abu, 2-aminobutyric acid) residue-specific bonded parameters.
; Copied VERBATIM from charmm36-jul2022.ff/ffbonded.itp, where each line
; carries an "ABA" tag in its own comment -- nothing derived or analogised.
;
; pmx needs no help with the appearing side chain: _check_case sees the dummy
; CG (A=AAD, B=AAA) and correctly looks up the all-real B-state parameters.
; That lookup is CT1-CG321-CG331 -- ABA own CA-CB-CG angle -- which simply was
; not in this force field.  No chimeric or dummy-state terms are involved.
; Only the entries this tree lacks are written, so no directive is duplicated.

[ angletypes ]
     CT1    CG321    CG331     5   113.500000   488.272800   0.25610000      9338.69 ; PROT alkanes ABA DBB DBB DBB

[ dihedraltypes ]
   CG331    CG321      CT1        C     9     0.000000     0.836800     3 ; from CG2O1 CG311 CG321 CG321, PENALTY= 0.9 ABA DBB
     CT1    CG321    CG331     HGA3     9     0.000000     0.669440     3 ; PROT rotation barrier in Ethane (SF) ABA DBB
     HB1      CT1    CG321    CG331     9     0.000000     0.836800     3 ; PROT alkane update, adm jr., 3/2/92 ABA DBB
     NH1      CT1    CG321    CG331     9     0.000000     0.836800     3 ; from NG2S1 CG311 CG321 CG321, PENALTY= 0.9 ABA DBB
